# mesh.cam — camp-3 mesh finishing fixture (ROADMAP Phase 4).
# Raster drop-cutter (z-map) finishing of an STL triangle mesh: serpentine XY
# passes, and at every sample the ball-nose centre rides the upper envelope of
# the ball-drop contact over all triangles. This is the ONE finishing path that
# accepts tessellation + sampling error (DECISIONS.md "Camp-3 slice 1…") — the
# analytical camps reject it.
#
# The mesh is a hand-written 4-triangle open square pyramid: base 40x40 at z=0,
# apex at (20,20,10) in model coords, so every golden number is hand-checkable.
# With the placement below and a dia-8 ball (r=4), the raster grid runs
# (6..54)^2 at step 2 (25x25 samples) and the apex lands exactly on the sample
# at (30,30): centre Z there = 10 + 4 = 14.0. Grid corners are beyond the
# ball's reach and clamp to the floor: Z = 0 + 4 = 4.0.
units mm
feed 600
plunge 200
rapid_z 5
clearance_z 30
spindle 4000

stock Box(w=60, l=60, h=15, x=0, y=0, z=0)

tool T9 Ballmill(dia=8.0)

# STL vertices are mm by definition (DECISIONS.md); x/y/z place the mesh in
# stock coords — base spans (10..50)^2, apex at (30,30,10).
feature Blob Mesh(file="pyramid.stl", x=10, y=10, z=0)

# stepover is both the Y row spacing and the X sample spacing
# (parse::derive_mesh_sample_step — one isotropic error budget).
run Copy(tool=T9, surface=Blob, stepover=2.0)
